 ## Operating characteristics
 
-*   **Time Complexity**: Not given in the sources.
-*   **Memory Complexity**: Not given in the sources.
-*   **Communication Overhead**: Communication is limited to copying the volume to shared memory (once per operation) and copying partial results from GPU to shared memory (once per worker) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths**:
-    *   Simple load balancing by partitioning angles [S1, unofficial].
-    *   Leverages TIGRE's optimized CUDA kernels [S1, unofficial].
-    *   Shared memory avoids network overhead in single-node multi-GPU setups [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations**:
-    *   Requires all GPUs to be accessible via shared memory, limiting deployment to single-node or specific cluster configurations [S1, unofficial].
-    *   Volume must fit in shared memory on all nodes [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to Use**: Ideal for single-node multi-GPU systems where the volume fits in memory and the bottleneck is the projection/backprojection speed [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When Not to Use**: When the volume is too large to fit in shared memory or when distributed across multiple networked nodes [S1, unofficial].
